{"id": "the-knowing-beast", "ids": "⿰犭⿻者丶", "title": "The Knowing Beast", "pronunciation": "zhě", "bopomofo": "ㄓㄜˇ", "meaning": "A domesticated animal that has learned to recognize or understand human intentions.", "formation": "phono-semantic", "definitions": [{"zh": "能識主人意之犬獸", "en": "A dog or beast capable of recognizing its master's intentions"}, {"zh": "通曉人情之馴獸", "en": "A tamed animal that understands human emotions"}, {"zh": "喻指善解人意者", "en": "Metaphorically, one who is perceptive of others' feelings"}], "etymology": "In ancient times, when the boundary between human and animal consciousness seemed more permeable, there existed a character for those rare beasts who transcended mere training to achieve true understanding. The dot above 者 suggests the spark of recognition—that moment when an animal's eyes reveal not just obedience, but comprehension. This character vanished as we forgot that wisdom could wear fur.", "source": {"work": "《說文解字》", "gloss": "⿰犭⿻者丶，識主之獸也。從犬，者聲。陟野切。"}, "components": [{"char": "犭", "meaning": "dog/beast"}, {"char": "者", "meaning": "者"}, {"char": "丶", "meaning": "丶"}], "examples": [{"text": "老犬⿰犭⿻者丶然，每聞主足音便迎於門", "translation": "The old dog was perceptive, greeting at the door whenever it heard its master's footsteps", "style": "classical"}, {"text": "此馬頗⿰犭⿻者丶，能察騎者之意而行止", "translation": "This horse is quite understanding, able to sense the rider's intentions and act accordingly", "style": "contemporary"}], "related": [{"char": "狗", "pinyin": "gǒu", "gloss": "dog"}, {"char": "識", "pinyin": "shí", "gloss": "recognize, know"}, {"char": "靈", "pinyin": "líng", "gloss": "intelligent, spiritual"}], "tags": ["animals", "consciousness", "domestication", "recognition"], "svg": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 512 512\" width=\"512\" height=\"512\">\n<style>@import url(\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Noto+Serif+TC:wght@400;700&display=swap\");</style>\n<g transform=\"translate(26.65,71.96) scale(0.310240,0.460093) 